## Critical assessment `v0.0.217` **passed the protocol smoke**. The earlier `v0.0.216` failure was a wrong-conversation problem. In this run, the request, response, and parsed reply are all tied to the same conversation: ```text conversation_id: 6a062d16-35f4-8387-9217-1d2bd9dde63f ``` The top-level result is clean: ```text ok: true status: reply_validated reply_status: no_artifact result_type: no_change reply_validation_ok: true artifact_candidate_count: 0 ``` The baseline continuity also looks correct: ```text input_artifact: chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.217.zip input_version: v0.0.217 registry_current: chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.217.zip target_version: v0.0.218 release_type: normal ``` The reply echoed the expected request/correlation id and returned a valid `promptbranch.ask.reply` envelope with `status: no_artifact`. fileciteturn10file0 ## Important caveat There is still one cosmetic/diagnostic weakness: ```text ask_response.answer: "Thinking\n\nStreaming interrupted. Waiting for the complete message..." ``` That field is not the final validated reply. The final parsed protocol reply is present at top level under `reply`, and validation passed. So this is **not blocking**, but I would keep it as a later cleanup: `ask_response.answer` should ideally reflect the final parsed answer or be clearly marked as an intermediate browser-stream value. ## Result classification ```text v0.0.217 protocol smoke: PASS wrong-conversation regression: FIXED for this run artifact creation: none, as expected source/artifact mutation: none, as expected baseline continuity: OK ``` ## Next step Run full validation before final acceptance: ```bash pb test full --json 2>&1 | tee pb_test.full.v0.0.217.log pb test report pb_test.full.v0.0.217.log --json \ | python3 -m json.tool ``` Then check package hygiene: ```bash zipinfo -1 .pb_profile/artifacts/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.217.zip \ | grep -E '(^|/)(\.pytest_cache|__pycache__)(/|$)|\.pyc$|\.log$|session_.*|task_.*' \ || echo "OK: no obvious generated/cache/log files" ``` ## Confidence High. The smoke JSON shows a validated protocol reply, correct baseline echo, no artifact candidates, and no wrong-conversation mismatch. ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — `v0.0.217` fixes the live protocol-smoke failure class and validates a `no_artifact` reply correctly. ⚠️ Weaknesses — `ask_response.answer` still contains an intermediate “Streaming interrupted” placeholder, which could confuse diagnostics. 🔍 Unknowns — full browser/agent/package test status after install. 🧩 Next step — run `pb test full` and `pb test report`; accept `v0.0.217` only if those are green.

