ed conversation still contained old turns, and the backend transcript snapshot was unchanged. The selected answer text was the previous assistant response, not a fresh reply to request id: ```text req_20260515T173458464829Z ``` So the likely failure is: ```text submit clicked / composer cleared, but ChatGPT did not persist a new user message ``` or: ```text Promptbranch refreshed/read the transcript before the new turn materialized and did not retry long enough through the backend source ``` ## Next diagnostic command Capture the service logs around this exact run: ```bash docker ps docker logs <promptbranch-service-container-id> --since=20m \ > promptbranch-service_v0.0.220_protocol_after_adopt_stale.log ``` Also inspect the debug classification file: ```bash python3 -m json.tool \ .pb_profile/ask_records/req_20260515T173458464829Z/classification.json ``` And the backend snapshots: ```bash cat .pb_profile/ask_records/req_20260515T173458464829Z/after_backend_snapshots.jsonl \ | python3 -m json.tool ``` ## v0.0.221 likely scope If the service log confirms the same pattern, `v0.0.221` should be narrow: ```text protocol submit materialization hardening ``` In scope: ```text - after composer clears, require backend message-count or latest-user-id change before answer parsing - if no backend change, perform one controlled target-conversation reload and re-read - distinguish: - submit_clicked_but_user_turn_not_persisted - submit_clicked_backend_snapshot_unchanged - submit_clicked_dom_loaded_old_turns_only - include explicit retry/exhaustion diagnostics - do not parse ask_response.answer when no fresh request message exists ``` Non-goals: ```text - no artifact/source/adoption changes - no protocol schema changes - no MCP policy changes - no rate-limit telemetry changes ``` ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — baseline continuity is now correct; stale-answer guard worked and prevented unsafe parsing. ⚠️ Weaknesses — fresh user turn did not persist/materialize after submit, so protocol smoke still fails. 🔍 Unknowns — whether this was a transient ChatGPT UI/backend issue or a deterministic v0.0.220 regression from the navigation/history reduction changes. 🧩 Next step — inspect the service log and ask debug records for `req_20260515T173458464829Z`; if confirmed, implement `v0.0.221` as protocol submit materialization hardening from `v0.0.220`.

