[294] assistant
Implemented `v0.0.221` from the pinned baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.220.zip ``` ## Critical assessment The failing `v0.0.220.after_adopt` smoke showed the correct baseline, but no new backend user message materialized after submit: ```text message_count_delta: 0 request_message_found: false newer_user_message_count: 0 latest_user_message_id_changed: false fingerprint_changed: false status: stale_answer_detected ``` So the fix had to protect the **pre-submit and fresh-turn boundary**, not artifact state or protocol schema. fileciteturn17file0 ## What changed in `v0.0.221` Added protocol ask hydration/materialization hardening: ```text - Force `chat-home-after-login` conversation navigations to reload instead of using the same-URL no-op skip. - Before filling/submitting a protocol ask, verify the target conversation DOM has hydrated. - If the target conversation remains zero-turn after one explicit reload, refuse submit with: target_conversation_not_hydrated_before_submit - Tightened fresh-turn evidence: old prompt-prefix matches no longer count as a fresh protocol request after a pre-ask marker. - Added clearer classification for old/already-loaded turns: submit_clicked_old_turns_only ``` Preserved: ```text - protocol schema - ask_response.answer normalization - source upload behavior - artifact intake behavior - adoption/release-control behavior - MCP/write policy - rate_limit_summary behavior ``` ## Validation From extracted release ZIP: ```text VERSION = v0.0.221 py_compile OK 253 focused tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 203 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 ``` ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip) ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — directly targets the stale-answer/materialization failure while preserving the `v0.0.220` rate-limit improvements. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live browser validation is still required; this cannot prove ChatGPT backend persistence from the sandbox. 🔍 Unknowns — whether one forced reload is enough for all slow-hydration cases. 🧩 Next step — install `v0.0.221`, rerun protocol smoke targeting `v0.0.222`, then run full test/report if the smoke is green.

