entionally blocked. So this track is here: ```text MCP Phase 1: done MCP Phase 2: done enough MCP Phase 3: guarded/limited MCP Phase 4: done enough MCP Phase 5: not yet ``` ✅ Good enough to support the ask/reply MVP. ⚠️ Not ready for autonomous write/release agents. --- ## Stage 2 — Ask/Reply protocol reliability **Status: now validated in `v0.0.221`.** This is what the recent releases were mostly about. The Ask/Reply design says automation must use the validated JSON envelope, not prose, and must fail closed if the reply is missing, invalid, ambiguous, or inconsistent. fileciteturn18file11 `v0.0.221` now proves: ```text pb ask --protocol works reply envelope validates request_id/correlation_id match baseline continuity works after adoption fresh user turn materializes wrong/stale conversation issues are guarded ask_response.answer is no longer treated as authoritative no_artifact smoke works ``` The full report confirms: ```text version: v0.0.221 browser.failure_count: 0 agent.failure_count: 0 suite.failure_count: 0 package_hygiene.ok: true version_consistency.ok: true rate_limit_summary.status: none ``` fileciteturn20file0 ✅ This stage is complete enough. --- ## Stage 3 — Artifact candidate detection / intake **Status: this is where we are now.** This is the next real MVP stage. The design doc’s target is not merely to validate a reply. It is to turn the reply into an inspectable artifact-intake workflow: ```text validated reply → artifact candidates → download decision → ZIP verification → candidate migration → test/adopt gate ``` fileciteturn18file11 Right now, our latest smoke only proves the `no_artifact` branch: ```text reply_status: no_artifact artifact_candidate_count: 0 result_type: no_change ``` That is necessary, but it is the simple path. What we have **not yet fully proven** is the release-producing path: ```text ChatGPT returns ZIP candidate → Promptbranch detects candidate → operator inspects candidate → operator downloads → Promptbranch verifies ZIP hygiene → candidate migrates → tests/adoption remain gated ``` So the current stage is: ```text Entering Artifact Intake MVP. ``` Not yet finished. --- # Stage map | MVP area | Current status | Meaning | |---|---:|---| | Workspace/task/artifact model | ✅ Stable | Core abstraction is clear | | Backend-first / transactional rules | ✅ Stable | Used as operating principle | | MCP read-only tools | ✅ Implemented | Local deterministic capability exists | | Skills | ✅ Implemented enough | Read-only skill guidance exists | | Ollama | ⚠️ Constrained | Proposal/summarization only | | Controlled process tool | ✅ Implemented | `test.smoke` works under policy | | Ask/reply protocol | ✅ Validated | `v0.0.221` proves stable protocol smoke | | Artifact candidate extraction | 🟡 Next | Needs MVP hardening now | | Download/verify/migrate candidate | 🟡 Next after extraction | Must remain operator-controlled | | Test/adopt candidate | 🟡 Existing pieces, needs integration | Must continue using existing release gates | | Autonomous source/artifact writes | ❌ Not yet | Explicitly out of scope for now | --- # What `v0.0.222` should be I would revise the `v0.0.222` scope to: ```text v0.0.222 — artifact-intake MVP inspection path ``` Not: ```text hygiene-only release ``` ## Core goal After a protocol ask, the operator should be able to inspect what Promptbranch thinks the reply means: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json ``` or equivalent. For a smoke/no-artifact reply, it should return: ```json { "ok": true, "status": "no_artifact", "artifact_candidate_count": 0, "next_action": "none" } ``` For a future release-producing reply, it should return: ```json { "ok": true, "status": "artifact_candidates_found", "artifact_candidate_count": 1, "next_action": "download_verify", "candidates": [ { "filename": "chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip", "role": "candidate_release", "version": "v0.0.222" } ] } ``` ## Guardrails still required Generated artifact/log/cache hygiene should remain an acceptance criterion, not the main feature. So `v0.0.222` should still verify: ```text no .pb_profile/ask_records in ZIP no ask_protocol_runs in ZIP no release logs no session logs no pycache / pytest cache no wrapper folder ``` But the main MVP value should be artifact-intake visibility. --- # Verdict ✅ Strengths — we have passed the fragile protocol/submission stage; `v0.0.221` is a credible baseline. ⚠️ Weaknesses — we have only proven the `no_artifact` branch, not the artifact-producing branch. 🔍 Unknowns — how much artifact-intake code already exists versus needs hardening around the latest protocol records. 🧩 Next step — define `v0.0.222` as **Artifact Intake MVP: inspect last validated protocol reply and classify artifact candidates**, with hygiene kept as a release gate.

