## v0.0.222 scope — Artifact Intake MVP inspection path Assumed accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip ``` Target: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip ``` ## Critical assessment This should be a **core MVP release**, not a hygiene-only release. `v0.0.221` proved the protocol ask/reply path: protocol smoke passed after adoption, full browser and agent suites passed, package hygiene passed, version consistency passed, and no rate-limit events were observed. fileciteturn20file0 The design docs say the target loop is: ```text pb ask structured request → ChatGPT answers with structured reply envelope → Promptbranch extracts and validates reply envelope → Promptbranch extracts artifact candidates → Promptbranch downloads artifacts only when explicitly requested → Promptbranch verifies ZIPs before migration → Promptbranch migrates verified ZIPs as candidate releases → Promptbranch tests/adopts only after green validation → next pb ask continues from the verified/adopted baseline ``` fileciteturn18file11 We have now validated the first half: ```text pb ask structured request → validated reply envelope → no_artifact branch ``` We still need to harden the next layer: ```text validated reply → inspect/classify artifact candidates ``` So `v0.0.222` should implement the **inspection/classification** part of artifact intake, without yet making download/migration/adoption automatic. --- # v0.0.222 MVP goal Add a reliable operator-safe command that reads the latest validated protocol reply and classifies the artifact-intake state. Recommended command: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json ``` Alternative acceptable naming if existing CLI shape prefers it: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-protocol-run --dry-run --json ``` But the command must be explicit that it is reading the **latest validated protocol reply**, not scraping arbitrary assistant prose. --- # Required behavior ## Case 1 — no artifact reply For the current protocol-smoke style answer: ```json { "status": "no_artifact", "artifacts": [] } ``` Expected output: ```json { "ok": true, "action": "artifact_intake", "mode": "dry_run", "status": "no_artifact", "source": "last_validated_protocol_reply", "reply_status": "no_artifact", "artifact_candidate_count": 0, "candidates": [], "next_action": "none", "download_performed": false, "migration_performed": false, "adoption_performed": false } ``` ## Case 2 — artifact candidate reply For a future reply containing: ```json { "status": "completed", "result_type": "release_candidate", "artifacts": [ { "kind": "zip", "filename": "chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip", "version": "v0.0.222", "role": "candidate_release", "download": { "available": true, "url": "..." } } ] } ``` Expected dry-run output: ```json { "ok": true, "action": "artifact_intake", "mode": "dry_run", "status": "artifact_candidates_found", "source": "last_validated_protocol_reply", "artifact_candidate_count": 1, "candidates": [ { "kind": "zip", "filename": "chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip", "version": "v0.0.222", "role": "candidate_release", "download_available": true, "baseline_ok": true, "filename_ok": true, "version_ok": true } ], "next_action": "download_verify", "download_performed": false, "migration_performed": false, "adoption_performed": false } ``` --- # In scope ## 1. Locate the latest protocol run Read from the existing protocol run/debug storage, for example: ```text .pb_profile/ask_protocol_runs/<request_id>.json .pb_profile/ask_records/<request_id>/reply.parsed.json ``` Selection rule: ```text latest successfully validated protocol reply only ``` Reject or warn on: ```text - no protocol run found - latest run not validated - missing reply block - reply_validation_ok is false - multiple ambiguous latest records ``` ## 2. Classify artifact-intake state Statuses should include at minimum: ```text no_artifact artifact_candidates_found invalid_reply missing_reply ambiguous_artifacts unsupported_artifact_type baseline_mismatch ``` ## 3. Validate artifact metadata For each candidate, validate: ```text kind == zip role in candidate_release / repair_candidate filename matches project naming convention version matches target/output version baseline input matches current accepted baseline download availability is explicit ``` For this project: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_<version>.zip ``` Example: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip ``` ## 4. Preserve fail-closed behavior If the reply is inconsistent, do not download, migrate, adopt, or update state. Output must be diagnostic only unless an explicit future download flag is used. ## 5. Keep hygiene as release gate `v0.0.222` must not package: ```text .pb_profile/ask_records/ .pb_profile/ask_protocol_runs/ .pb_profile/release_logs/ pb_ask_protocol_smoke*.json pb_test.full*.log pb_test_report*.json session_*.log task_*.txt __pycache__/ .pytest_cache/ *.pyc ``` --- # Explicit non-goals Do **not** implement automatic: ```text - artifact download - candidate migration - candidate adoption - Project Source mutation - source sync changes - release-control adoption changes - MCP write/process policy changes ``` Do **not** change: ```text - ask/reply protocol schema - ask_response.answer normalization - fresh-turn materialization logic - conversation-lock logic - rate-limit pacing logic ``` --- # Tests to add Focused tests: ```text test_artifact_intake_no_artifact_from_last_validated_reply test_artifact_intake_finds_zip_candidate test_artifact_intake_rejects_invalid_reply test_artifact_intake_rejects_baseline_mismatch test_artifact_intake_rejects_unsupported_artifact_type test_artifact_intake_dry_run_does_not_download_migrate_or_adopt test_artifact_intake_uses_latest_validated_protocol_run test_release_zip_excludes_protocol_debug_records ``` Fixtures: ```text tests/fixtures/artifact_intake/ no_artifact_reply.json release_candidate_reply.json baseline_mismatch_reply.json invalid_artifact_type_reply.json ``` --- # Acceptance criteria `v0.0.222` is acceptable if: ```text - built from chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip only - VERSION and package metadata = v0.0.222 - pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json works for no_artifact - artifact candidate fixture/classification tests pass - dry-run performs no download, migration, adoption, source mutation, or state advancement - protocol smoke passes targeting v0.0.223 - full test/report passes - package_hygiene.ok = true - version_consistency.ok = true - ZIP has no wrapper folder and no generated/debug/cache artifacts ``` Suggested validation: ```bash pb ask "Protocol smoke only. Return a valid promptbranch.ask.reply envelope with status no_artifact. Do not create a ZIP." \ --protocol \ --from-current-baseline \ --target-version v0.0.223 \ --parse-reply \ --protocol-timeout-seconds 120 \ --protocol-fresh-turn-timeout-seconds 60 \ --protocol-fresh-turn-poll-seconds 2 \ --json \ | tee .pb_profile/release_logs/v0.0.222/pb_ask_protocol_smoke.v0.0.222.json pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json \ | tee .pb_profile/release_logs/v0.0.222/pb_artifact_intake_dry_run.v0.0.222.json pb test full --json 2>&1 | tee pb_test.full.v0.0.222.log pb test report pb_test.full.v0.0.222.log --json \ | tee pb_test_report_pb_test.full.v0.0.222.log.json \ | python3 -m json.tool ``` ## Confidence High. This is the correct next MVP step because it extends the already validated protocol layer into the next designed stage: artifact candidate inspection. It avoids the unsafe jump to automatic download/migration/adoption. ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — keeps MVP momentum, builds directly on validated `v0.0.221`, and implements the next designed artifact-intake stage. ⚠️ Weaknesses — still does not complete full artifact intake; download/verify/migrate remains future work. 🔍 Unknowns — exact current storage API for “last validated protocol reply” needs code inspection during implementation. 🧩 Next step — implement `v0.0.222` from `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip` as **Artifact Intake MVP inspection/classification only**, with hygiene as a hard release gate.

