[361] assistant
Implemented `v0.0.222` from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.221.zip ``` ## What changed `v0.0.222` implements the **Artifact Intake MVP inspection/classification path**. Main behavior: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json ``` now reads the latest validated protocol-run record from: ```text .pb_profile/ask_protocol_runs/ ``` and classifies the reply as: ```text no_artifact artifact_candidates_found baseline_mismatch missing_reply invalid_reply protocol_run_not_found ``` For `no_artifact`, it reports: ```text status: no_artifact artifact_candidate_count: 0 next_action: none download_performed: false migration_performed: false adoption_performed: false ``` For candidate replies, it reports candidate metadata and keeps the next action explicit: ```text status: artifact_candidates_found next_action: download_verify download_performed: false migration_performed: false adoption_performed: false ``` ## Guardrails preserved No changes to: ```text pb ask protocol schema reply parsing semantics ask_response.answer normalization source upload/sync behavior artifact adoption behavior MCP write/process policy rate-limit pacing ``` Dry-run does **not** download, migrate, adopt, mutate Project Sources, or advance state. ## Hygiene hardening Release ZIP hygiene now explicitly rejects `.pb_profile/` debug/protocol artifacts, including: ```text .pb_profile/ask_records/ .pb_profile/ask_protocol_runs/ .pb_profile/release_logs/ ``` The generated release ZIP has: ```text VERSION = v0.0.222 entry_count = 202 ZIP CRC/testzip OK wrapper_folder = false bad_generated_entry_count = 0 hygiene_count = 0 ``` ## Validation Passed: ```text py_compile OK 238 focused tests passed extracted-ZIP verification tests passed: 6/6 ZIP hygiene check passed ``` ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.zip) ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — moves the MVP forward from validated protocol replies to artifact-intake classification. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live protocol smoke and full browser/agent validation still need to run locally after install. 🔍 Unknowns — whether future real artifact-producing ChatGPT replies expose stable downloadable URLs or require browser-mediated download later. 🧩 Next step — install `v0.0.222`, run protocol smoke targeting `v0.0.223`, then run `pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json` and full test/report.

