## v0.0.223 proposed scope Accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.1.zip ``` Target: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.223.zip ``` `v0.0.222.1` is accepted because the post-release validation helper passed all gates: artifact current, protocol smoke, artifact intake dry-run, full test/report, and ZIP hygiene all returned `rc: 0` with `failure_count: 0`. fileciteturn21file0 ## Critical assessment `v0.0.222` implemented the **inspection/classification** part of Artifact Intake MVP. `v0.0.222.1` only added the reusable post-release validation script; it did not advance the MVP slice. The ask/reply protocol design defines the intended artifact flow as: ```text validated reply → artifact candidates → explicit download → ZIP verification → candidate migration → test/adopt gate → next ask from adopted baseline ``` The design also says downloaded artifacts must not become accepted baselines immediately; they must move through candidate states first. fileciteturn21file11 So the next correct MVP step is **not adoption** yet. It is: ```text explicit artifact candidate download + ZIP verification ``` --- # Recommended v0.0.223 scope ## Theme ```text Artifact Intake MVP — explicit download and ZIP verification ``` ## Goal Extend: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json ``` into an explicit operator-controlled download/verify path: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --json ``` This command should download only validated ZIP artifact candidates from the latest validated protocol reply, verify the ZIP, and store it as a local candidate/inbox artifact. It must **not** migrate, adopt, upload, or advance state. --- # In scope ## 1. Explicit candidate download Only allow download when all of these are true: ```text - latest protocol run is validated - reply_validation_ok is true - artifact_candidate_count >= 1 - artifact kind is zip - artifact role is candidate_release or repair_candidate - artifact filename matches project naming convention - artifact version matches reply baseline.output_version / target version - download.available is true - direct URL is present, or a supported local/download reference exists ``` For this project, expected filename pattern: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.223.zip ``` ## 2. Artifact inbox / candidate storage Downloaded artifacts should go into a clearly non-accepted location, for example: ```text .pb_profile/artifact_inbox/ ``` or: ```text .pb_profile/artifact_candidates/ ``` Expected record: ```json { "status": "downloaded_verified", "candidate_ref": "chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.223.zip", "candidate_version": "v0.0.223", "accepted": false, "migrated": false, "adopted": false } ``` ## 3. ZIP verification Verification must include at minimum: ```text - file exists - file is a ZIP - zipfile.testzip passes - no wrapper folder - repo contents are at ZIP root - VERSION exists - VERSION matches candidate version - pyproject / package version matches candidate version if present - no nested ZIPs - no .pb_profile/ - no ask_records/ - no ask_protocol_runs/ - no release_logs/ - no session logs - no pb_test logs - no __pycache__/ - no .pytest_cache/ - no *.pyc / *.pyo ``` ## 4. Fail-closed statuses Add clear statuses: ```text no_artifact artifact_candidates_found download_verified download_failed download_url_missing unsupported_artifact_type artifact_filename_mismatch artifact_version_mismatch artifact_baseline_mismatch zip_verification_failed zip_hygiene_failed ``` ## 5. Dry-run remains safe Existing dry-run behavior must remain unchanged: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --dry-run --json ``` It must still report candidates without downloading anything. ## 6. No state advancement The command must explicitly report: ```json { "download_performed": true, "verification_performed": true, "migration_performed": false, "adoption_performed": false, "project_source_mutated": false, "artifact_registry_updated": false, "state_artifact_updated": false, "state_source_updated": false } ``` --- # Explicit non-goals Do **not** implement yet: ```text - candidate migration to repo root - artifact adoption - Project Source upload - source sync changes - release-control adoption changes - automatic test/adopt - automatic continuation from candidate - MCP write/process policy changes - protocol schema changes ``` Do **not** loosen the `direct_url_only` policy unless the design is updated explicitly. --- # Tests to add Focused unit/fixture tests: ```text test_artifact_intake_download_verify_zip_candidate test_artifact_intake_download_requires_explicit_flag test_artifact_intake_download_rejects_missing_url test_artifact_intake_download_rejects_non_zip test_artifact_intake_download_rejects_filename_mismatch test_artifact_intake_download_rejects_version_mismatch test_artifact_intake_verify_rejects_wrapper_folder test_artifact_intake_verify_rejects_nested_zip test_artifact_intake_verify_rejects_pb_profile_debug_artifacts test_artifact_intake_download_does_not_migrate_or_adopt ``` Fixture layout: ```text tests/fixtures/artifact_intake/ release_candidate_with_url.json release_candidate_missing_url.json release_candidate_filename_mismatch.json valid_candidate_zip.zip wrapper_folder_candidate_zip.zip dirty_candidate_zip.zip ``` --- # Acceptance criteria `v0.0.223` is acceptable only if: ```text - built from chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.1.zip - VERSION and package metadata = v0.0.223 - dry-run artifact intake still works for no_artifact - fixture-based artifact candidate download/verify passes - missing/invalid URL fails closed - bad ZIP hygiene fails closed - no migration/adoption/source mutation occurs - protocol smoke passes targeting v0.0.224 - post-release-validation script passes - full test/report passes - ZIP hygiene passes ``` Suggested validation: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.223 \ --target-version v0.0.224 ``` And a specific artifact-intake candidate test command if implemented: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --json ``` For no-artifact smoke replies, expected output remains: ```json { "ok": true, "status": "no_artifact", "artifact_candidate_count": 0, "download_performed": false, "migration_performed": false, "adoption_performed": false } ``` --- # Why this is the right next MVP step `v0.0.221` stabilized protocol ask/reply. `v0.0.222` made the latest validated reply inspectable and classifiable. `v0.0.222.1` made the validation loop repeatable. So `v0.0.223` should advance the next designed transition: ```text artifact candidate → downloaded verified candidate ``` Not: ```text candidate → accepted baseline ``` That would skip too much risk control. ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — advances the core Artifact Intake MVP while preserving explicit operator control. ⚠️ Weaknesses — real ChatGPT artifact URLs may be inconsistent; missing URL must fail closed. 🔍 Unknowns — whether current protocol replies expose stable direct-download URLs for ZIP artifacts. 🧩 Next step — implement `v0.0.223` from `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.222.1.zip` as **explicit artifact candidate download + ZIP verification only**, with no migration or adoption.

