Implemented `v0.0.224` from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.223.zip ``` `v0.0.223` was accepted because post-release validation passed with `failure_count: 0` across artifact current, protocol smoke, artifact intake dry-run, full test/report, and ZIP hygiene. fileciteturn22file0 ## What changed `v0.0.224` implements: ```bash pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --migrate --json ``` New supported flow: ```text validated protocol reply → candidate classification → explicit ZIP download → ZIP verification → migrate verified candidate ZIP to repo root → register candidate in .pb_profile/artifact_candidates.json → stop ``` No adoption is performed. ## Guardrails preserved The migration step requires: ```text - a selected artifact candidate - successful ZIP verification - source ZIP located inside .pb_profile/artifact_inbox/ - valid repo root - safe basename ZIP filename - clean ZIP hygiene ``` It explicitly does **not** perform: ```text - adoption - Project Source upload - source sync - artifact-current baseline update - source-current baseline update - release-control test/adopt ``` The result reports: ```text migration_performed: true candidate_registry_updated: true adoption_performed: false project_source_mutated: false artifact_registry_updated: false state_artifact_updated: false state_source_updated: false ``` ## Validation Passed from worktree: ```text py_compile OK artifact intake / protocol / parser tests passed container / MCP / shell-script tests passed ``` Passed from extracted ZIP: ```text VERSION = v0.0.224 py_compile OK focused artifact-intake migration tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 205 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 ``` ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.224.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.224.zip) ## Next step Install `v0.0.224`, then run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.224 \ --target-version v0.0.225 ```

