## Critical assessment `v0.0.224` is acceptable as the current baseline. The post-release validation summary shows: ```text ok: true failure_count: 0 version: v0.0.224 target_version: v0.0.225 ``` All required gates returned `rc: 0`: ```text artifact_current artifact_intake_dry_run protocol_smoke test_full test_report zip_hygiene ``` So the verified-candidate-migration slice passed its release gate. fileciteturn24file0 ## Acceptance decision Accept: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.224.zip ``` as the current baseline. Future development should continue from: ```text v0.0.224 ``` not from `v0.0.223`. ## Where we are now in the Artifact Intake MVP You have now covered: ```text v0.0.222 → inspect/classify latest validated protocol reply v0.0.223 → explicit candidate download + ZIP verification v0.0.224 → verified candidate migration only, no adoption ``` The design target sequence is: ```text validated reply → artifact candidates → explicit download → ZIP verification → candidate migration → test/adopt gate → continue from adopted baseline ``` The next missing stage is therefore **not another migration change**. It is the **candidate test gate**. The ask/reply protocol design explicitly separates candidate artifacts from accepted baselines and says downloaded/migrated artifacts must not become accepted automatically. fileciteturn24file11 ## Recommended next scope Define `v0.0.225` as: ```text Artifact Intake MVP — migrated candidate test gate, no adoption yet ``` Scope: ```text pb artifact candidate test --json ``` or equivalent existing command shape. It should: ```text - locate the latest migrated candidate - verify candidate registry metadata - verify candidate ZIP still exists - verify ZIP hygiene again - run a controlled validation/test command against the candidate - write a candidate test result record - report candidate_test_status - not adopt - not upload Project Source - not update artifact_current/source_current ``` Explicitly out of scope for `v0.0.225`: ```text - no adoption - no Project Source mutation - no source sync - no automatic baseline advancement - no protocol schema changes ``` ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — `v0.0.224` passed all release gates and completes the “verified candidate migration only” slice. ⚠️ Weaknesses — candidate migration exists, but the migrated candidate is not yet independently test-gated. 🔍 Unknowns — exact preferred CLI name for candidate testing should be checked against current code before implementation. 🧩 Next step — define and implement `v0.0.225` from `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.224.zip` as **migrated candidate test gate only, with no adoption**.

