[604] assistant
You were right. I corrected this as a second repair release. ## Implemented repair Built: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.225.2.zip ``` from the repair line, correcting the bad `v0.0.225.1` behavior. [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.225.2.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.225.2.zip) ## What changed `post-release-validation.sh` now treats `artifact_current` semantic mismatch as **diagnostic by default**, not as a validation failure. So this no longer fails just because the artifact is not adopted yet: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.225.2 \ --target-version v0.0.226 ``` The script still records the mismatch under: ```text artifact_current_semantic.rc: 1 ``` but the total validation can still pass. ## New explicit adoption mode Added: ```bash --adopt-if-accepted ``` Expected workflow: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.225.2 \ --target-version v0.0.226 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` Behavior: ```text 1. Run validation gates. 2. If all gates pass, run: pb artifact adopt chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.225.2.zip --from-project-source --json 3. Re-run artifact current. 4. Fail only if post-adoption semantic state still does not match v0.0.225.2. ``` ## Strict mode preserved Added/kept a strict option for workflows that really do require prior adoption: ```bash --require-adopted-baseline ``` That mode fails if: ```text state.artifact_version != --version state.source_version != --version registry_current.version != --version ``` ## Validation performed Passed: ```text bash -n scripts/post-release-validation.sh py_compile OK 6 version-surface focused tests passed post-release validation default mismatch diagnostic test passed post-release validation require-adopted failure test passed post-release validation adopt-if-accepted test passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK wrapper_folder = false bad_entry_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.225.2 ``` Note: the three post-release-validation tests pass individually; running them as one pytest group appears to hang because of the shell/process-substitution logging pattern in the script test harness, not because the tested behavior fails. ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — validation and adoption are now separated correctly. ⚠️ Weaknesses — the script test harness still exposes a process-lifetime awkwardness when grouped under pytest. 🔍 Unknowns — live `--adopt-if-accepted` still needs to be run locally against your real Promptbranch state. 🧩 Next step — install `v0.0.225.2`, then run post-release validation with `--adopt-if-accepted`.

