Implemented `v0.0.226` from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.225.2.zip ``` ## What changed `pb artifact accept-candidate` is now a **tested-candidate adoption gate**. It now requires: ```text migrated candidate ZIP → ZIP verified → candidate registry selected → existing candidate-test record exists → candidate-test result passed → then local artifact/source baseline adoption ``` It no longer runs release-control itself. Specifically: ```text --run-release-control ``` is now rejected for `accept-candidate` in `v0.0.226`. ## Guardrails preserved No changes to: ```text Project Source upload source sync ask/reply protocol schema artifact intake download/verify/migrate candidate-test execution MCP policy browser/source mutation behavior ``` `--from-project-source` remains optional verification only. It does **not** upload or mutate Project Sources. ## Validation performed From worktree and extracted ZIP: ```text VERSION = v0.0.226 py_compile OK 182 focused CLI/parser/artifact tests passed 18 version-surface/container/test-suite focused tests passed 50 extracted-ZIP candidate-adoption/parser tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 207 wrapper_folder = false bad_entry_count = 0 ``` I did not claim a full live browser/post-release validation pass inside the sandbox. That still needs to run locally. ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.zip) ## Next step Install `v0.0.226`, then run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.226 \ --target-version v0.0.227 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — completes tested-candidate adoption as a separate gate. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live post-release validation is still required before acceptance. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke and local adoption result for `v0.0.226`. 🧩 Next step — run post-release validation with `--adopt-if-accepted`.

