ash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.226.1 \ --target-version v0.0.227 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ## If it fails again with the same status Then `v0.0.226.1` needs a narrow repair: ```text v0.0.226.2 ``` Repair scope only: ```text post-release-validation / protocol ask hydration hardening ``` Likely fix: ```text when target_conversation_not_hydrated_before_submit: - wait longer for conversation turns - reload target conversation once - re-check backend/DOM agreement - retry submit only if the target conversation is hydrated - preserve fail-closed behavior if hydration still fails ``` Do not advance to `v0.0.227` until this is green. ## Verdict ✅ Strengths — baseline is correct and the submit was safely blocked before an unsafe protocol ask. ⚠️ Weaknesses — browser conversation hydration remains flaky under post-release validation. 🔍 Unknowns — whether this was a one-off hydration miss or a deterministic timeout in long conversations. 🧩 Next step — rerun protocol smoke once; if the same hydration error repeats, build `v0.0.226.2` as a narrow hydration-retry repair.

