Implemented repair release: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.2.zip ``` Built from: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.1.zip ``` ## Why this repair was needed `v0.0.226.1` repeatedly failed protocol smoke before submit with: ```text target_conversation_not_hydrated_before_submit ``` The baseline was correct, but the browser-side conversation had no hydrated visible turns, so Promptbranch safely refused to submit. fileciteturn34file0 ## What changed Narrow repair only: ```text promptbranch_browser_auth/client.py chatgpt_browser_auth/client.py tests/test_project_list_browser_client.py docs/repair-v0.0.226.2.md README.md UPGRADING.md version metadata ``` Hydration gate now: ```text - waits longer by default before protocol submit - performs up to 2 bounded recovery reloads - waits for post-reload settle/network idle when available - records reload_count, max_reload_attempts, timeout_ms, final DOM turn counts - still refuses to submit if the target conversation remains unhydrated ``` No changes to: ```text ask/reply protocol schema artifact intake candidate-test accept-candidate Project Source upload source sync MCP policy ``` ## Validation performed Passed: ```text py_compile changed modules 38 project-list/browser-client tests 59 focused parser/version/container/MCP tests extracted-ZIP focused repair tests ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 210 wrapper_folder = false bad_entry_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.226.2 ``` ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.2.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.226.2.zip) ## Next step Install `v0.0.226.2`, then run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.226.2 \ --target-version v0.0.227 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — keeps fail-closed behavior while making hydration recovery less brittle. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live browser validation still needs to run locally. 🔍 Unknowns — whether two reloads are enough for this long conversation under current ChatGPT UI behavior. 🧩 Next step — run post-release validation with `--adopt-if-accepted`; accept only if protocol smoke passes post-adoption.

