[874] assistant
## Critical assessment `v0.0.229` is built from: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.228.zip ``` I kept it inside the Artifact Intake MVP. The design direction says the artifact flow should move from validated reply → artifact candidates → download/verify/migrate → test/adopt → continue from adopted baseline, with automation using validated protocol data rather than prose. fileciteturn37file10 ## Implemented v0.0.229 Added the high-impact read-only MVP command: ```bash pb artifact candidate-next --json ``` Purpose: ```text Inspect the current artifact candidate lifecycle → choose exactly one safest next operator action → return the recommended command → perform no mutation ``` It can work across all candidates: ```bash pb artifact candidate-next --json ``` or for one selected candidate: ```bash pb artifact candidate-next --version v0.0.229 --json ``` ## Why this matters for the MVP Before this release, the operator could inspect lifecycle state with: ```bash pb artifact candidate-status --all --json ``` but still had to interpret the inventory manually. Now `candidate-next` turns that inventory into one deterministic next command, for example: ```text pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --migrate --json pb artifact candidate-test --version vX.Y.Z --json pb artifact accept-candidate --version vX.Y.Z --adopt-if-green --json pb artifact current --json ``` ## Guardrails preserved `candidate-next` is strictly read-only. It does **not** perform: ```text download verification write migration candidate-test execution adoption Project Source upload artifact/source state advancement protocol schema change browser/source behavior change ``` ## Validation performed Passed from worktree and extracted ZIP: ```text py_compile OK candidate-next tests passed candidate-status regression tests passed accept-candidate regression tests passed CLI parser test passed container/version focused tests passed MCP initialize/version focused test passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 210 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.229 ``` I did **not** claim live browser/post-release validation inside the sandbox. ## Release artifact [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.229.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.229.zip) ## Next step Install and run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.229 \ --target-version v0.0.230 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — big MVP usability gain: one read-only command now decides the next safe candidate lifecycle step. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live post-release validation still required before accepting `v0.0.229`. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke and adoption result for `v0.0.229`. 🧩 Next step — validate `v0.0.229`; accept only if post-release validation passes.

