## Implemented `v0.0.230` Built from: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.229.zip ``` Release artifact: [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.230.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.230.zip) ## Big MVP step Added: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --json ``` This is the next step after `candidate-next`. The purpose is to close the MVP operator loop: ```text inspect candidate lifecycle → choose the safest next step → optionally execute exactly one allowlisted step → stop ``` This stays aligned with the MVP design: Promptbranch should drive artifact intake through validated candidate stages, not free-form prose or uncontrolled automation. The design explicitly defines the flow as candidate → downloaded → verified → migrated → tested → adopted, with fail-closed validation between stages. fileciteturn38file10 ## New command behavior Plan only, default: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --json ``` Execute exactly one next step: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --execute-next --json ``` For a selected candidate: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --version v0.0.230 --json pb artifact candidate-run --version v0.0.230 --execute-next --json ``` ## Guardrails `candidate-run` does **not** invent new mutation behavior. It only executes one of the already-existing lifecycle commands: ```text artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --migrate artifact candidate-test artifact accept-candidate --adopt-if-green artifact current ``` It does not add: ```text Project Source upload protocol schema changes browser automation changes unchecked adoption new release-control behavior source sync changes ``` This follows the operating model that Promptbranch is the local control plane while ChatGPT remains the execution surface, with transactional writes and backend/verified state as the authority. fileciteturn38file3 ## Validation performed Passed: ```text py_compile OK candidate-run tests passed candidate-next regression tests passed candidate-status regression tests passed accept-candidate regression tests passed CLI parser test passed container/version focused tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 209 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.230 ``` ## Next step Install and run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.230 \ --target-version v0.0.231 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — this is a real MVP step: one command now plans or executes the next safe candidate lifecycle step. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live post-release validation still needs to run locally. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke and adoption result for `v0.0.230`. 🧩 Next step — validate `v0.0.230`; accept only if post-release validation passes.

