[963] assistant
## Critical assessment In `v0.0.230`: **no**, `pb artifact candidate-run --json` was **not** tested by `scripts/post-release-validation.sh`. That was a validation gap because `candidate-run` is now the command that closes the operator loop for the Artifact Intake MVP. The MVP design says the candidate flow must move through validated stages before adoption, and automation must use validated state rather than prose. fileciteturn39file10 ## Implemented `v0.0.231` Built from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.230.zip ``` Release artifact: [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.231.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.231.zip) ## What changed `post-release-validation.sh` now includes: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --json ``` as a **plan-only** release gate. It does **not** use: ```bash --execute-next ``` So post-release validation still does not mutate candidate state, download artifacts, test candidates, or adopt candidates through `candidate-run`. The summary now includes: ```json "artifact_candidate_run_plan": { "phase": "pre_adoption | post_adoption", "rc": 0 } ``` Added: ```bash --skip-candidate-run ``` for rare diagnostic runs only. Also fixed a small script robustness issue: ```text pb command resolution now exits immediately if neither promptbranch nor pb is found. ``` ## Why this is a big MVP step This makes the final Artifact Intake MVP command part of the acceptance gate: ```text protocol smoke → artifact intake dry-run → candidate-run plan → tests/report → ZIP hygiene → optional adopt-if-accepted ``` In `--adopt-if-accepted` mode, `candidate-run` runs **after adoption, protocol smoke, and artifact intake dry-run**, so it validates against the adopted baseline context. This aligns with the operating model: Promptbranch is the local control plane, ChatGPT is the execution surface, and state-changing flows must be transactional and verified. fileciteturn39file3 ## Validation performed Passed: ```text bash -n scripts/post-release-validation.sh py_compile OK post-release-validation focused tests passed individually post-release-validation shell-script fake workflow passed candidate-run regression tests passed version/container/MCP focused tests passed extracted-ZIP focused tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 210 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.231 ``` I did not claim live browser/post-release validation inside the sandbox. ## Next step Install and run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.231 \ --target-version v0.0.232 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — `candidate-run` is now part of the release acceptance path. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live validation still needs to run locally. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke/adoption result for `v0.0.231`. 🧩 Next step — validate `v0.0.231`; accept only if post-release validation passes.

