## Implemented `v0.0.232` Built from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.231.zip ``` Release artifact: [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.232.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.232.zip) ## Big MVP step Added: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --execute-until-blocked --json ``` This is a significant step toward finalizing the Artifact Intake MVP because it closes the remaining operator loop: ```text plan next candidate step → execute allowlisted step → re-read lifecycle state → continue until accepted / blocked / failed / max-steps ``` This stays aligned with the MVP design: artifact candidates must move through validated stages before adoption, and automation must use validated state instead of prose. fileciteturn40file10 ## New behavior Plan-only remains default: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --json ``` One-step execution remains: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --execute-next --json ``` New bounded lifecycle mode: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run \ --execute-until-blocked \ --max-steps 4 \ --json ``` It executes only existing allowlisted lifecycle commands: ```text pb artifact intake --from-last-answer --download --verify --migrate --json pb artifact candidate-test --version <version> --repo-path <repo> --json pb artifact accept-candidate --version <version> --repo-path <repo> --adopt-if-green --json ``` It stops on: ```text accepted candidate failed step no allowlisted next step max-steps reached invalid mode ``` ## Guardrails preserved No changes to: ```text Project Source upload source sync browser automation ask/reply protocol schema candidate-test semantics accept-candidate semantics post-release validation mutation behavior ``` `post-release-validation.sh` still runs `candidate-run` in plan-only mode. The new lifecycle execution mode is explicit and operator-controlled. This follows the project’s control-plane model: Promptbranch controls workflow and policy, while state-changing paths must remain transactional and verified. fileciteturn40file3 ## Validation performed Passed: ```text py_compile OK candidate-run --execute-until-blocked tests passed candidate-run invalid-mode tests passed candidate-next regression tests passed candidate-run --execute-next regression tests passed CLI parser tests passed promptbranch CLI version test passed MCP initialize/version test passed container/API version focused tests passed extracted-ZIP focused tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 211 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.232 ``` I did not claim live browser/post-release validation inside the sandbox. ## Next step Install and run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.232 \ --target-version v0.0.233 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — major MVP usability step: one explicit command can now drive the artifact-candidate lifecycle through existing gates until completion or block. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live post-release validation still needs to run locally. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke/adoption result for `v0.0.232`. 🧩 Next step — validate `v0.0.232`; accept only if post-release validation passes.

