## Implemented `v0.0.233` Built from accepted baseline: ```text chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.232.zip ``` `v0.0.232` is accepted because your post-release validation passed with `failure_count: 0`, adoption performed, post-adoption protocol smoke green, candidate-run plan green, full tests/report green, and ZIP hygiene green. fileciteturn41file0 Release artifact: [Download `chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.233.zip`](sandbox:/mnt/data/chatgpt_claudecode_workflow_v0.0.233.zip) ## Big MVP step Added **artifact-candidate MVP completion proof** to: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --json ``` New fields: ```text mvp_completion mvp_complete ``` Added strict gate: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --require-complete --json ``` This returns nonzero unless the lifecycle proves: ```text candidate accepted accepted candidate matches current artifact/source baseline registry current matches state artifact source state matches artifact state no adoption-ready candidate still pending no tested-but-unaccepted candidate still pending no verified-but-untested candidate still pending ``` This closes an important MVP gap: after `candidate-run --execute-until-blocked`, the operator now gets a machine-readable proof that the candidate lifecycle is actually complete, not just that commands ran. The design requires the candidate pipeline to move through explicit verified stages before adoption. fileciteturn42file12 ## New usage Plan/check only: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run --require-complete --json ``` Execute lifecycle and require final proof: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run \ --execute-until-blocked \ --require-complete \ --max-steps 4 \ --json ``` For one candidate: ```bash pb artifact candidate-run \ --version v0.0.233 \ --execute-until-blocked \ --require-complete \ --json ``` ## Guardrails preserved No changes to: ```text Project Source upload source sync browser automation ask/reply protocol schema candidate-test semantics accept-candidate semantics post-release validation mutation behavior ``` `--require-complete` is an assertion/gate. It does not create a new mutation path. ## Validation performed Passed: ```text py_compile OK candidate-run require-complete incomplete test passed candidate-run require-complete after-acceptance test passed candidate-run execute-until-blocked regression passed candidate-run execute-next regression passed CLI parser tests passed promptbranch CLI version test passed MCP initialize/version test passed container/API version focused tests passed extracted-ZIP focused tests passed ZIP CRC/testzip OK entry_count = 210 wrapper_folder = false hygiene_count = 0 VERSION = v0.0.233 ``` I did not claim live browser/post-release validation inside the sandbox. ## Next step Install and run: ```bash scripts/post-release-validation.sh \ --version v0.0.233 \ --target-version v0.0.234 \ --adopt-if-accepted ``` ✅ Strengths — `candidate-run` now has a scriptable MVP completion proof, not only execution status. ⚠️ Weaknesses — live post-release validation still needs to run locally. 🔍 Unknowns — live protocol smoke/adoption result for `v0.0.233`. 🧩 Next step — validate `v0.0.233`; accept only if post-release validation passes.

